# Tank Tactics - Core Context

Combined-arms arena roguelite for browser and Android. A run starts with one player tank versus one AI tank at 120 HP. Players paste a restricted Python subset for individual unit scripts and an optional squad script. Hero units are future work only.

## Layout

- `client/` - browser game, UI, combat renderer, scripts, styles
- `local/` - local server, multiplayer, model connectors, build scripts, tests
- `cloud/` - server worker and Python policy
- `drizzle/` - append-only database migrations
- `dist/` - generated output, committed with source changes (never hand-edit)
- `android/` - Android wrapper and build scripts
- `docs/` - scripting reference sources

## Non-negotiable product constraints

- The first battle stays one player tank versus one AI tank at 120 HP.
- Scripted Python is a bounded data subset. It must never execute arbitrary Python or grant units, gear, upgrades, score, or resources.
- Model connections are optional and opt-in. Provider keys stay in memory; never commit, log, or include them in prompts.
- Preserve mobile usability and verify controls at narrow phone widths when changing UI.
- Keep hero units on the roadmap unless the product owner changes that decision.

`AGENTS.md` holds the full guide. Read it before large changes.
